+- $A_{sub} \in \mathbb{R}^{M \times (R_i + p)}$: The randomly selected submatrix formed by extracting $R_i + p$ columns from $A$ [S1][S2, unofficial].
+
+**Numbered Steps:**
+1. Randomly select $R_i + p$ distinct column indices from $\{1, \dots, N\}$ [S1][S2, unofficial].
+2. Extract the columns of $A$ indexed by the selection set to form the submatrix $A_{sub}$ [S1][S2, unofficial].
+3. Compute the SVD of $A_{sub}$ to obtain its left singular vectors [S1][S2, unofficial].
+4. Check if $A_{sub}$ has full rank. If not, the selected columns do not contain $R_i$ linearly independent vectors; select a new set of random columns and repeat from Step 1 [S1][S2, unofficial].
+5. If $A_{sub}$ has full rank, return the first $R_i$ left singular vectors as the approximation [S1][S2, unofficial].
+
+**Formulas:**
+- $A_{sub} = A[:, \mathcal{I}]$, where $\mathcal{I} \subset \{1, \dots, N\}$ and $|\mathcal{I}| = R_i + p$ [S1][S2, unofficial].
+- $A_{sub} = U_{sub} \Sigma_{sub} V_{sub}^T$ via SVD decomposition [S1][S2, unofficial].
+- $U_{sub} \in \mathbb{R}^{M \times R_i}$ contains the first $R_i$ left singular vectors [S1][S2, unofficial].
 
